<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">26092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Russian attacks on Kyiv killed five people on Friday, one of them a child, and Mayor Vitali Klitschko says forty-three more were injured, twenty-five of them taken to hospital.</s> <s>A daytime drone struck an office building in the Solomianskyi district, and three bodies were found in its parking lot.</s> <s>On the same day, Vladimir Putin told reporters that every peace proposal was still on the table... and put the blame on Kyiv.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>All four of Iraq's airports, from Baghdad and Najaf in the south to Erbil and Sulaimaniya in the north, have now stopped flights to and from Iran.</s> <s>Washington didn't have to ban anything inside Iraq, because ground-service firms reportedly won't risk secondary American sanctions and being cut off from dollar clearing, the same lever that's kept Iraq's oil revenue flowing through New York since the two thousand three invasion.</s> <s>Pilgrims bound for Najaf, students and patients now face a land journey of at least twelve hours, while Tehran's seven-day ceasefire proposal still waits for an American reply.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Pakistan's Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, residents of the mountainous Hathikhel area of Bannu say militants are demanding up to a hundred thousand rupees and a share of their crops before families can leave, and that the homes of those who fled without paying have been torn down.</s> <s>Bannu itself sheltered hundreds of thousands of people who fled North Waziristan's military operation in two thousand fourteen, and now its own families are leaving, one household at a time, with no camp and no count.</s> <s>Elders say security operations are pushing people out from the other side too... and the longer families stay away, the more they fear their farmland won't be theirs to come back to.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kazakhstan has detained five naval officers, including the navy's first deputy commander, on suspicion of negligence, after fourteen of seventeen servicemen swept into the Caspian Sea died.</s> <s>Twelve of the dead were conscripts, carried away as they got off the vessel Kaisar into water that was only a metre deep.</s> <s>Negligence is the charge for now, but grieving families will want to know who sent young conscripts into the sea in those conditions, and whether the inquiry will go further up the chain of command.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United States Supreme Court has let states check their voter rolls against a federal citizenship database called SAVE, just weeks before the midterm elections.</s> <s>Texas officials had already found that it wrongly flagged five hundred and seventy-eight citizens, yet the court's unsigned emergency order gave no reasoning, and all three liberal justices dissented.</s> <s>Naturalised citizens whose immigration and Social Security records don't match may not find out they've been removed until they turn up to vote.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Namibia has built Africa's first zero-emissions iron plant, and experts say Southern Africa could make green steel together, breaking a pattern from the colonial era in which ore leaves the region and finished steel comes back.</s> <s>South Africa's steelworks have closed and its first green steel ventures have stumbled, but it still has deep-water ports and mountains of iron ore waste, while Namibia has cheap renewable hydrogen.</s> <s>Whether neighbouring governments can share grids, water and ports across their borders will decide if that value finally stays at home.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Italy's Eni will cap its own pump prices for thirty days from Monday, holding diesel at two euros nineteen a litre and petrol at one euro ninety-nine, about seventeen cents below the national average.</s> <s>The company blames the closure of nearly thirty European refineries in fifteen years, along with the shutdown of Hormuz, which has pushed Brent crude close to a hundred and fifteen dollars, up almost a quarter in a month.</s> <s>Because Eni's partly state-owned, the open question is who really absorbs the margin it's giving up... and whether independent stations nearby can survive the comparison.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Bolivia, the UN drug office says coca cultivation has hit a record, with sixty-five and a half percent more leaf in the ground than the law allows.</s> <s>The Cochabamba Tropics is licensed for seven thousand seven hundred hectares, but it planted seventeen thousand four hundred and seventy last year and sold less than a tenth of its leaf on the legal market.</s> <s>That surplus could feed up to two hundred and seventy-five tonnes of cocaine, which is a hard test for a country that expelled American drug agents in two thousand eight and promised to manage coca on its own terms.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Volkswagen is recalling two point eight six million cars over a single bolt that can corrode, fracture and cause steering failure, according to Germany's transport authority.</s> <s>The recall covers Tiguan, Touran, Golf and Caddy models built between two thousand thirteen and two thousand twenty-four, plus seven hundred thousand Audis.</s> <s>Sharing parts across models is how carmakers cut costs, and it's also how one small flaw ends up under millions of drivers at the same time.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ebola has now killed three thousand seven hundred and seventy-nine people in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, according to Africa's disease control agency.</s> <s>That's already more than the country's two thousand eighteen epidemic in the same eastern provinces, and while cases in Ituri fell by a quarter, North Kivu's rose fifty-six percent in just three weeks.</s> <s>Insecurity is blocking the search for cases, so tracers are finding only twenty contacts per patient against a target of sixty, and nobody can say yet where this outbreak ends.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Antarctic sea ice peaked this winter at seventeen point five nine million square kilometres, the third-smallest peak in forty-eight years of satellite records.</s> <s>Researcher Clare Eayrs says the five lowest July extents on record have all come since two thousand twenty-two, and the four lowest Augusts since two thousand twenty-three.</s> <s>For decades the ice around Antarctica held steady or even grew, against what climate models expected... so scientists are now asking whether it's shifted into a new, lower state for good.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Belgian firm, Space Applications Services, has booked a twenty-kilogram rover on a Blue Origin lander bound for the Moon.</s> <s>More than half a century after the Soviet Lunokhod became the first robot to drive on the lunar surface, this would be Europe's first fully commercial rover mission, paid for by customers rather than space agencies.</s> <s>Public money built the design, but the flight depends on payload reservations and operations contracts, so the real experiment is whether a lunar business model can hold up.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Physicists now widely accept holography, the idea that everything inside a region of space, gravity included, can be rebuilt from information on its surface.</s> <s>It grew out of the nineteen seventies discovery that a black hole's information scales with the area of its horizon rather than its volume, and its three founding papers are the most cited theoretical physics work of the digital age.</s> <s>What they still argue about is what it means for reality... whether space itself is fundamental, or something that emerges from deeper quantum connections.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Apple has withdrawn its strongest iCloud encryption, known as Advanced Data Protection, from new users in Britain after a government order under the two thousand sixteen Investigatory Powers Act, which critics call the Snoopers' Charter.</s> <s>As a result, two identical iPhones in the UK can now offer different levels of security, depending only on when their owners switched the feature on.</s> <s>It shows how a state can weaken encryption without ever legislating a backdoor, simply by making strong encryption commercially unviable in its market.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's Geely says its new battery charges from ten to seventy percent in four and a half minutes, about as long as it takes to fill a petrol tank.</s> <s>The pack can take in two point two megawatts, compared with the six hundred kilowatt ceiling of the fastest American chargers, and Geely credits artificial intelligence thermal control that keeps the battery near fifty-five degrees.</s> <s>For electric cars, the bottleneck is moving from the battery to the grid behind it, and China's building that as well.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>